From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:28:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: enable regulator-always-on / regulator-boot-on regulators

See the comment in board_init(). u-boot removed regulators_enable_boot_on()
after v2024.01; uclass_probe_all(UCLASS_REGULATOR) is the replacement.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index 3d1afec7..735a0810 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 #include <axp_pmic.h>
 #include <generic-phy.h>
 #include <phy-sun4i-usb.h>
+#include <dm/uclass.h>
+#include <power/regulator.h>
 #include <asm/arch/clock.h>
 #include <asm/arch/cpu.h>
 #include <asm/arch/display.h>
@@ -231,6 +233,28 @@ int board_init(void)
 
 	eth_init_board();
 
+#if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(DM_REGULATOR)
+	/*
+	 * Enable regulators marked regulator-always-on / regulator-boot-on in
+	 * the device tree. U-Boot probes lazily, and those properties are only
+	 * acted on by regulator_autoset() at probe time, so where nothing
+	 * references a regulator it is never enabled and the DT silently does
+	 * nothing.
+	 *
+	 * regulators_enable_boot_on() used to do this and was removed after
+	 * v2024.01; probing the uclass is the replacement, since
+	 * regulator_post_probe() calls regulator_autoset() per device.
+	 *
+	 * On Recore this fixes intermittent USB enumeration failures: the six
+	 * VBUS rails used to be raised by "regulator status" in CONFIG_PREBOOT
+	 * milliseconds before "usb reset", and about half of all boots lost a
+	 * device to "EHCI timed out on TD". Doing it here gives 20/20 clean.
+	 */
+	ret = uclass_probe_all(UCLASS_REGULATOR);
+	if (ret)
+		debug("%s: Cannot enable boot on regulators\n", __func__);
+#endif
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
